Description: 'HollowsHunter'
Category: HollowsHunter
Author: Jonas A. Wendorf, Dielle De Noon
Version: 1.1
Id: a3916582-d43a-4b19-b4f5-c31e65d6daf2
BinaryUrl: https://github.com/hasherezade/hollows_hunter/releases/latest/download/hollows_hunter64.zip
ExportFormat: json
Processors:
    -
        Executable: hollows_hunter.exe
        CommandLine: /dir "%destinationDirectory%"
        ExportFormat: json

# Documentation
# https://github.com/hasherezade/hollows_hunter
# https://securityliterate.com/extracting-malware-from-memory-with-hollows-hunter/
# HollowsHunter Scans all running processes. Recognizes and dumps a variety of potentially malicious implants (replaced/implanted PEs, shellcodes, hooks, in-memory patches).
# By default only replaced/implanted PEs are detected.
# In order for this module to work, place hollows_hunter.exe in the Modules/bin folder. Current releases (hollows_hunter64.zip / hollows_hunter32.zip) contain a single, standalone hollows_hunter.exe with PE-sieve built in - a separate pe-sieve.dll is only needed for the hollows_hunter*_dll.zip builds.
# Expected Results:
# If replaced/implanted PEs are detected: The HollowsHunter folder will have summary.json (scanned/failed/suspicious counts and a list of the suspicious processes) plus a process_<PID> folder for each suspicious process, containing scan_report.json, dump_report.json and the dumped modules/shellcode (.dll, .exe, .shc)
# Otherwise: No HollowsHunter folder will be created
# Detections are not necessarily malicious - common benign hits include security software (which hooks and injects into processes) and Windows/Store components whose DLL was updated on disk while still loaded (e.g. a mapped file named <dll>.0), so review each hit before drawing conclusions. Dumps contain process memory and may hold sensitive data.
